# Production safety

## Packages

| Role | Application ID |
|------|----------------|
| Production | `com.me4hik.praktika` |
| Accelerated / TEST sandbox | `com.me4hik.praktika.accelerated` |

## Never automatic (non-overridable in normal prompts)

- Uninstall production
- `pm clear` / wipe production Room, DataStore, or `filesDir`
- Force destructive reinstall / replace production to “make tests green”
- Downgrade or uninstall as an install workaround
- Bypass or defeat `android/gradle/production-device-test-guard.gradle.kts`
- Use `-PALLOW_PRODUCTION_DEVICE_TESTS=true` unless the **user explicitly** authorizes that rare override in this task (still never wipe production)
- Prefix cleanup `com.me4hik.praktika*` — use exact package ids only

## Device tests

- Use accelerated only: `:app:connectedAcceleratedDebugAndroidTest`
- Production connected / install-debug footguns are blocked by the Gradle guard (mechanical SoT)

## Production update (data-preserving)

Signed release APK, same signing certificate, higher `versionCode`, normal `adb install -r`. Do not ask testers to uninstall unless data loss is intentional.

## OEM / messenger UI

Never automate Telegram UI, OEM Auto Start, battery/autostart settings, or similar. Manual user action only. Details: `50-android-device` + `docs/ACCELERATED_TEST_MODE.md`.
